<?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="assets/xml/rss.xsl" media="all"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Colour Science</title><link>https://www.colour-science.org/</link><description>Colour: Colour Science for Python</description><atom:link href="https://www.colour-science.org/rss.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"></atom:link><language>en</language><copyright>Contents © 2026 &lt;a href="mailto:colour-developers@colour-science.org"&gt;Colour Developers&lt;/a&gt; </copyright><lastBuildDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:34:45 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>Nikola (getnikola.com)</generator><docs>http://blogs.law.harvard.edu/tech/rss</docs><item><title>Gaussian-Based Spectral Upsampling</title><link>https://www.colour-science.org/posts/gaussian-based-spectral-upsampling/</link><dc:creator>Colour Developers</dc:creator><description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered" id="cell-id=febbc4ae"&gt;&lt;div class="prompt input_prompt"&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="inner_cell"&gt;
&lt;div class="text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html"&gt;
&lt;h3 id="Introduction"&gt;Introduction&lt;a class="anchor-link" href="https://www.colour-science.org/posts/gaussian-based-spectral-upsampling/#Introduction"&gt;¶&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered" id="cell-id=7dbae1f54112cc7"&gt;&lt;div class="prompt input_prompt"&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="inner_cell"&gt;
&lt;div class="text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Spectral reflectance upsampling, or reflectance recovery, is the process of converting tristimulus values into spectral reflectance distributions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This document explores the Gaussian-based spectral upsampling method implemented in &lt;a href="https://github.com/colour-science/colour"&gt;Colour&lt;/a&gt; on the &lt;code&gt;develop&lt;/code&gt; branch as of this writing. The method uses clamped Gaussian basis spectra with the hierarchical decomposition algorithm from &lt;em&gt;Smits (1999)&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.colour-science.org/posts/gaussian-based-spectral-upsampling/"&gt;Read more…&lt;/a&gt; (9 min remaining to read)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description><category>colorchecker classic</category><category>colour</category><category>colour science</category><category>reflectance</category><category>RGB colourspace</category><category>spectral</category><guid>https://www.colour-science.org/posts/gaussian-based-spectral-upsampling/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Jan 2026 08:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Colour 0.4.7 is available!</title><link>https://www.colour-science.org/posts/colour-047-is-available/</link><dc:creator>Colour Developers</dc:creator><description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The colour-science Developers are pleased to announce the release of
&lt;a class="reference external" href="https://github.com/colour-science/colour/releases/tag/v0.4.7"&gt;Colour 0.4.7&lt;/a&gt;!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.colour-science.org/posts/colour-047-is-available/"&gt;Read more…&lt;/a&gt; (1 min remaining to read)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description><category>colour</category><category>colour science</category><category>release</category><guid>https://www.colour-science.org/posts/colour-047-is-available/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 06 Dec 2025 08:37:03 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Support for Color Exchange Format in Colour available!</title><link>https://www.colour-science.org/posts/support-for-cxf-in-colour-available/</link><dc:creator>Colour Developers</dc:creator><description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are happy to announce the release of &lt;a class="reference external" href="https://github.com/colour-science/colour-cxf"&gt;Colour - CxF&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This extension package for &lt;strong&gt;Colour&lt;/strong&gt; implements reading and writing files in the &lt;a class="reference external" href="https://www.xrite.com/page/cxf-color-exchange-format"&gt;Color Exchange Format (CxF)&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.colour-science.org/posts/support-for-cxf-in-colour-available/"&gt;Read more…&lt;/a&gt; (1 min remaining to read)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description><category>colour</category><category>colour cxf</category><category>colour science</category><category>cxf</category><category>release</category><guid>https://www.colour-science.org/posts/support-for-cxf-in-colour-available/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 24 Sep 2025 09:50:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Support for Common LUT Format in Colour available!</title><link>https://www.colour-science.org/posts/support-for-clf-in-colour-available/</link><dc:creator>Colour Developers</dc:creator><description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are happy to announce the release of &lt;a class="reference external" href="https://github.com/colour-science/colour-clf-io"&gt;Colour - CLF IO&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This extension package for &lt;strong&gt;Colour&lt;/strong&gt; implements reading and writing files in the &lt;strong&gt;Common LUT Format (CLF)&lt;/strong&gt;, as well as
using Colour to execute  workflows defined in CLF.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.colour-science.org/posts/support-for-clf-in-colour-available/"&gt;Read more…&lt;/a&gt; (1 min remaining to read)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description><category>clf</category><category>colour</category><category>colour clf io</category><category>colour science</category><category>release</category><guid>https://www.colour-science.org/posts/support-for-clf-in-colour-available/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Apr 2025 12:47:44 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Colour 0.4.5 is available!</title><link>https://www.colour-science.org/posts/colour-045-is-available/</link><dc:creator>Colour Developers</dc:creator><description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The colour-science Developers are pleased to announce the release of
